## Description

This is a revamp of the `connectAutocomplete` connector leveraging scoped results (#3964). 

Since this is a complete rewrite of how the connector works, I took this opportunity to migrate it to TypeScript.

### Options changes

The [`indices`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/autocomplete/js/#connector-param-render-indices) option doesn't exist anymore and is inferred by the widgets tree. If the option is used in development mode, a warning is raised.

### Structure change of an autocomplete index

```diff
 interface AutocompleteIndex {
-  label: string;
   index: string;
   hits: Hits;
   results: SearchResults | undefined;
 }
```

Once we introduce the concept of index IDs, we might want to add it so that users can make a difference from indexes having the same name:

```diff
 interface AutocompleteIndex {
-  label: string;
+  indexId: string;
-  index: string;
+  indexName: string;
   hits: Hits;
   results: SearchResults | undefined;
 }
```

